# Copy this file to .env (or .env.local) and adjust for your setup.
#
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# VITE_API_BASE_URL — where the frontend sends API/WebSocket requests.
#
# If you leave this UNSET, the frontend auto-detects it from whatever
# hostname/IP you used to open the page (see src/services/apiClient.ts):
#   opened as http://localhost:5173   -> assumes backend at http://localhost:8000
#   opened as http://192.168.1.66:5173 -> assumes backend at http://192.168.1.66:8000
# That default is correct for the common case (backend + frontend on the
# same machine, reached over LAN by IP) and needs no .env file at all.
#
# Only set this explicitly if the backend lives somewhere else — a
# different host, a non-default port, or behind HTTPS/a reverse proxy.
#
# Example for this project's typical LAN setup (PC running backend+frontend
# at 192.168.1.66, ESP32/phones/laptops on the same WiFi):
# VITE_API_BASE_URL=http://192.168.1.66:8000

# VITE_API_BASE_URL=
